   "title": "Russia Starts Towing Ship Hit by Drones in Baltic, Finland Says",
   "url": "https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2026/11/22/russian-cargo-ship-still-on-fire-off-finland-after-attack-a94343",
   "domain": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "source": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "published": "Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:26:00 +0300",
   "_dt": 1795364760.0,
   "ageDays": 0.09,
   "summary": "A fire onboard a Russia n cargo ship that was struck by drones in the Baltic Sea continued to burn through the night even as efforts were made to douse the flames, Finland's coast guard said on Sunday. Ukraine has sent waves of military drones towards Russia 's northwest coastal Leningrad region this year, including some that strayed into the airspace of nearby Baltic countries, leading to fears that the war was spilling onto NATO territory.",
   "summary_zh": "芬兰海岸警卫队周日表示，一艘在波罗的海遭无人机袭击的俄罗斯货船起火后，火势整夜持续燃烧，工作人员正努力灭火。今年以来，乌克兰多次向俄罗斯西北沿海的列宁格勒地区派遣军事无人机，其中一些还误入邻近波罗的海国家领空，引发了战争可能蔓延至北约领土的担忧。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "A fire onboard a Russia n cargo ship that was struck by drones in the Baltic Sea continued to burn through the night even as efforts were made to douse the flames, Finland's coast guard said on Sunday. The Finnish military has said the strike on the Sparta II on Saturday was likely carried out by Ukraine and that the vessel later drifted into Finnish waters where it remains at anchor. The 16 crew members were evacuated onto a nearby Russia n ship. Pictures and video released by the coast guard showed several vessels spraying the Sparta II with water cannons during the night in a bid to put out the flames and cool down containers stacked on its deck. Ukraine has sent waves of military drones towards Russia 's northwest coastal Leningrad region this year, including some that strayed into the airspace of nearby Baltic countries, leading to fears that the war was spilling onto NATO territory. The ship, bound for Russia n exclave Kaliningrad, was damaged in international waters west of Russia 's Gogland island, Finland's Defense Forces have said, corroborating an account by Russia n officials. The risk of further attacks in the Gulf of Finland, a narrow arm of the Baltic Sea, cannot be ruled out, Estonian Navy Commander Ivo Vark told public broadcaster ERR on Sunday. Finland's military said last week it had detected a strike on a Russia n warship in the same area during Ukrainian drone attacks. The Sparta II is a 121-meter Russia n-flagged cargo vessel owned by Russia n shipping company Oboronlogistika that left St. Petersburg on Friday, according to LSEG data. The vessel is subject to U.S. sanctions, according to the U.S. Treasury Department. Oboronlogistika provides logistics services for the Russia n Defense Ministry, according to the company's website. We are facing unprecedented challenges. Russia's Prosecutor General's Office has designated The Moscow Times as an \"undesirable\" organization, criminalizing our work and putting our staff at risk of prosecution. This follows our earlier unjust labeling as a \"foreign agent.\" These actions are direct attempts to silence independent journalism in Russia. The authorities claim our work \"discredits the decisions of the Russian leadership.\" We see things differently: we strive to provide accurate, unbiased reporting on Russia. We, the journalists of The Moscow Times, refuse to be silenced. But to continue our work, we need your help . Your support, no matter how small, makes a world of difference. If you can, please support us monthly starting from just $ 2. It's quick to set up, and every contribution makes a significant impact. By supporting The Moscow Times, you're defending open, independent journalism in the face of repression. Thank you for standing with us",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ru"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
