   "ageDays": 0.1,
   "summary": "The Chamber of Licensed Gold Buyers (CLGB) has underscored the importance of strategic investment in infrastructure, financing and sector formalisation to support Ghana’s ambition of refining 70 per cent of artisanal and small-scale mining (ASM) gold locally by December 2027. In its policy position on the 2027 Budget, the Chamber welcomed the Government’s strategic direction to transition Ghana from the export of raw minerals towards greater domestic refining, value addition and industrial development.",
   "summary_zh": "持牌黄金买家商会（CLGB）强调，为支持加纳到2027年12月在本国精炼70%的手工采矿业及小规模采矿业（ASM）黄金这一目标，对基础设施、融资和行业正规化进行战略投资至关重要。在有关2027年预算的政策立场中，该商会欢迎政府推动加纳从出口原矿转向扩大国内精炼、增值和工业发展的战略方向。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "The Chamber of Licensed Gold Buyers (CLGB) has underscored the importance of strategic investment in infrastructure, financing and sector formalisation to support Ghana’s ambition of refining 70 per cent of artisanal and small-scale mining (ASM) gold locally by December 2027. In its policy position on the 2027 Budget, the Chamber welcomed the Government’s strategic direction to transition Ghana from the export of raw minerals towards greater domestic refining, value addition and industrial development. CLGB considers this ambition a significant opportunity to deepen local participation in the gold value chain, strengthen national economic resilience and maximise the developmental benefits of the country’s mineral resources. The Chamber notes that, based on its current estimates, approximately 30 per cent of ASM gold is refined locally. Achieving the 70 per cent target would therefore req",
