   "title": "Nigeria, US Deepen Maritime Security Ties, Target Illegal Movement Of Strategic Goods",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/nigeria-us-deepen-maritime-security-ties-target-illegal-movement-of-strategic-goods/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:23:15 +0000",
   "_dt": 1795116195.0,
   "ageDays": 2.97,
   "summary": "Speaking at the engagement, the Customs Area Controller, Edo/Delta Area Command, Deputy Comptroller Dominic Dooyum Ortsen, described the initiative as timely, given the strategic responsibility of the Service in safeguarding Nigeria’s borders and ensuring compliance with national laws and international security obligations.",
   "summary_zh": "在这场交流活动上，海关埃多/三角洲地区司令部副关长、助理关务专员Dominic Dooyum Ortsen表示，考虑到尼日利亚海关肩负着守护国家边境、确保遵守国家法律以及履行国际安全义务的战略职责，这项举措十分及时。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Speaking at the engagement, the Customs Area Controller, Edo/Delta Area Command, Deputy Comptroller Dominic Dooyum Ortsen, described the initiative as timely, given the strategic responsibility of the Service in safeguarding Nigeria’s borders and ensuring compliance with national laws and international security obligations. Ortsen said the responsibilities of the Customs Service went beyond revenue collection, trade facilitation and suppression of smuggling, noting that growing security challenges in the maritime sector required stronger intelligence gathering, risk profiling and identification of strategic and dual-use goods. He stressed the need for specialised training and sustained capacity development for officers involved in maritime security, cargo examination and enforcement operations. The Customs chief also highlighted the introduction of Customs Mutual Assistance Agreements (CMA) as a framework for improving cooperation, information exchange and operational collaboration between customs administrations. He called for stronger inter-agency collaboration, improved technical capabilities and continuous professional development to address emerging maritime security threats. Ortsen said the engagement provided an opportunity for Nigerian and US representatives, alongside other relevant agencies, to exchange views on maritime security challenges and strengthen institutional cooperation. He reaffirmed the commitment of the Comptroller-General of Customs, Bashir Adewale Adeniyi, to equipping officers with the knowledge, technical skills and operational intelligence required to identify goods that could pose security risks. As part of the programme, participants toured relevant maritime and port facilities to gain practical insights into port operations, existing security arrangements and the responsibilities of different stakeholders in the maritime environment. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": true,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_leadership",
   "title_zh": "尼日利亚与美国深化海上安全关系，打击战略物资非法贩运",
   "body_zh": "在这次交流活动上，Edo/Delta区域指挥部海关区域主管、副司库级官员Dominic Dooyum Ortsen表示，考虑到海关部门在守护尼日利亚边境以及确保遵守国家法律和国际安全义务方面所承担的战略责任，这项举措十分及时。Ortsen指出，海关部门的职责 Beyond 征税、贸易便利化和打击走私，还包括其他方面；随着海上安全挑战不断增加，必须加强情报收集、风险画像分析，并识别战略物资和两用物。他强调，应对参与海上安全、货物查验和执法行动的人员开展专业培训，并持续提升其能力。这名海关负责人还highlighted 海关互助协议(CMA)的引入，认为该协议为改善各国海关当局之间的合作、信息交流和行动协作提供了框架。他呼吁加强跨机构协作、提升技术能力并持续开展专业培训，以应对新出现的海上安全威胁。Ortsen表示，此次交流活动为尼日利亚和美国代表以及其他相关机构提供了一个机会，就海上安全挑战交换意见，并加强机构合作。他重申了海关总司司长Bashir Adewale Adeniyi的承诺，即为官员配备识别可能构成安全风险货物所需的知识、技术技能和行动情报。作为活动的一部分，与会者参观了相关海上和港口设施，以实地了解港口运营、现有安全安排以及海上环境中不同利益相关方的职责。我们掌握独家优势。获取实时报道、突发新闻和独家视角，直接推送到您的手机。不要满足于过时资讯。加入LEADERSHIP NEWS的WhatsApp频道，随时获取全天候更新 →",
   "snippet_zh": ""
